cription":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of Colorado, including the following areas,\nCentral Colorado River Basin, Central Gunnison and Uncompahgre\nRiver Basin, Central Yampa River Basin, Debeque to Silt Corridor,\nFlat Tops, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, Gore and Elk\nMountains/Central Mountain Valleys, Grand Valley, Grand and\nBattlement Mesas, Northwest San Juan Mountains, Paradox\nValley/Lower Dolores River, Roan and Tavaputs Plateaus, Southwest\nSan Juan Mountains, Uncompahgre Plateau and Dallas Divide, Upper\nGunnison River Valley and West Elk and Sawatch Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains, Southeast\nUtah and Tavaputs Plateau.\n\n* WHEN...Through Monday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nRecent burn scars will also be especially susceptible and these\ninclude the Lee and Elk RX, Gold Mountain and Elk, Ferris, and\nBabylon burn scars to name a few.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Monsoonal moisture will remain across the area through Monday\nevening and will support thunderstorms and showers with heavy\nrainfall across the watch area. Several rounds of heavier rain\nare expected increasing the chance for flash flooding especially\nin our more susceptible areas.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-01T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Central Yampa River Basin; Roan and Tavaputs Plateaus; Grand Valley; Debeque to Silt Corridor; Central Colorado River Basin; Grand and Battlement Mesas; Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys; Central Gunnison and Uncompahgre River Basin; West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Flat Tops; Upper Gunnison River Valley; Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Southeast Utah; Tavaputs Plateau; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bf53ca765d0cc18c1b080bdda7ac3b081a211a37.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bf53ca765d0cc18c1b080bdda7ac3b081a211a37.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-30T21:01:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 302101 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 301 PM MDT Sun Aug 30 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Multiple rounds of showers and storms are expected today, especially along and north of I-70. - Another wet day is on tap tomorrow as well, with higher coverage of precipitation across southeast Utah and southwest Colorado. - Flash flooding is possible thr","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-30T20:47:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Multiple rounds of showers are expected between now and Monday evening. Heavy rain, gusty outflow winds, and lightning will be the biggest concerns. Temperatures drop thanks to increased cloud cover and precipitation. Fire weather concerns remain minimal. A downturn in precip is possible for Tuesday and beyond. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS.","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"oth01","station_name":"Olathe","distance_km":3.7,"soil_temp_5cm_f":81.37,"soil_temp_15cm_f":77.22,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":35,"wind_speed_mph":0.75,"air_temp_f":68.07,"relative_humidity":0.618,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/oth01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KMTJ","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KMTJ 302253Z AUTO 35005KT 10SM FEW047 FEW110 22/10 A3019 RMK AO2 LTG DSNT 